{{Enemy Infobox|Bronze Automaton}}
'''Bronze Automaton''' is a [[Boss]] found at the end of [[Act 2]].

== Pattern ==
{{Intents|Bronze Automaton}}
Always starts with {{Int|Bronze Automaton|Spawn Orbs}}, then repeats the following pattern:
#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|Flail}}
#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|Boost}}
#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|Flail}}
#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|Boost}}
#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|HYPER BEAM}}
#{{Int|Bronze Automaton|Stunned}}

On {{Asc|19|Ascension}}, '''Bronze Automaton''' will always use {{Int|Bronze Automaton|Boost}} in place of {{Int|Bronze Automaton|Stunned}}.

= Bronze Orb =
{{Enemy Infobox|Bronze Orb}}
{{Keyword Infobox|Stasis}}
'''Bronze Orb''' is a {{KW|Minion}} summoned only by the {{M|Bronze Automaton}}.

== Pattern ==
{{Intents|Bronze Orb}}
Each '''Bronze Orb''' can only use {{Int|Bronze Orb|Stasis}} once per combat. {{Int|Bronze Orb|Stasis}} has a 75% chance to be used each turn until it has been picked. After using {{Int|Bronze Orb|Stasis}} '''Bronze Orb''' has a 70% chance to use {{Int|Bronze Orb|Support Beam}} and a 30% chance to use {{Int|Bronze Orb|Beam}} each turn. '''Bronze Orb''' cannot use the same attack thrice in a row.
=== Stasis ===
{{Int|Bronze Orb|Stasis}} will always prioritize the highest [[Cards#Card Rarity|rarity]] Card in your draw pile. If your draw pile is empty, {{Int|Bronze Orb|Stasis}} will pick from your discard pile instead. Cards in {{KW|Stasis}} will not be affected by certain variables; for example, {{C|Masterful Stab}}'s {{KW|Energy}} cost will not increase even if the player takes damage.

{{Clear}}

